---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Panel from "../components/Panel.astro";
import { site } from "../site.js";
---
<Base title="Downloads" description="How to get the Skyline Tower content from the Steam Workshop and join the server.">
	<h1 class="page-heading">Download Center</h1>
	<div class="callout">
		<b>Everything you need is on the Steam Workshop.</b> No installers, no content packs to unzip, no toolbars. Ever.
	</div>

	<Panel title="Step 1: Subscribe to the Workshop collection">
		<p>Skyline Tower needs extra content (maps, models, sounds and textures) to look right. Open our Workshop collection and click <b>Subscribe to all</b>. Steam downloads everything and keeps it up to date for you.</p>
		<p class="center"><a class="btn btn-green" href={site.links.workshop}>Download</a></p>
	</Panel>

	<Panel title="Step 2: Mount Counter-Strike: Source (recommended)">
		<p>Some maps and props use CS:S content. If you own it, mount it from the Garry's Mod main menu (the controller icon at the bottom right). Without it, you'll see some pink-and-black checkerboards.</p>
	</Panel>

	<Panel title="Step 3: Join!">
		<p>Hit <b>Connect Now!</b> in the Server Status box, or open your console in Garry's Mod and type:</p>
		<p class="center"><code>connect {site.servers[0].address}</code></p>
	</Panel>

	<Panel title="Why Workshop?">
		<ul>
			<li>It's quick, compressed, and needs no extra programs.</li>
			<li>Updates download automatically.</li>
			<li>It's tied to your Steam account, so it comes back if you reinstall.</li>
			<li>It works on Windows, macOS and Linux.</li>
		</ul>
	</Panel>
</Base>
